    mode: "CRITICAL"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["GHOST-002", "GHOST-003", "PAT-003", "PAT-007", "PAT-017", "PAT-020"]
    l0_abstract: "Added shared SCRIBE state synchronization for Codex IDE, Codex CLI, and other local agents."
    pourquoi: "The multi-agent failure mode was not only concurrent writes; it was stale context after another agent wrote first. A tiny state file with a real writer object, current SCRIBE hash, changed IDs, and closed write_kind enum gives each agent a cheap preflight check without pretending to be a full orchestrator."
    validations:
      - "`scribe sync` reports missing or stale state without overwriting the last writer."
      - "`scribe sync --repair` atomically writes `scribe-out/state.json` with writer object, line count, hash, last session, changed IDs, and write_kind."
      - "`scribe whoami` displays the recorded writer from state.json."
