    mode: "STANDARD"
    hot_entries_consulted: ["VAC-008", "VAC-006", "PAT-024", "GHOST-003", "SCAR-002"]
    l0_abstract: "Fixed the persistent extension hydration mismatch by removing the manual root-layout head script."
    pourquoi: "The reported diff showed React comparing the app-owned inline cleanup script with a `chrome-extension://eppiocem...` script injected by the browser extension. The previous mitigation was directionally right about extension mutation but wrong about placing an app script in `<head>`; Next App Router root layouts should avoid manual head nodes, and the safer app-side boundary is a null-rendering client sanitizer inside `<body>` plus root suppressHydrationWarning."
    validations:
      - "Next local layout documentation checked: root layouts define html/body and should not manually add head tags."
      - "Removed manual `<head>` and `extension-hydration-cleanup` script from app/layout.tsx."
      - "Added ExtensionDomSanitizer client component scoped to known bis attributes and the observed extension script signature."
      - "frontend npm run lint passed."
      - "frontend npx tsc --noEmit passed."
      - "frontend npm run build passed."
      - "curl -I http://localhost:3000/login returned 200 OK."
      - "graphify update . rebuilt the application graph to 265 nodes and 203 edges."
      - "git diff --check passed."
